  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Objetos de todos los días**",
      "",
      "| Para escribir y estudiar | Electrónicos | Personales |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| book · pen · pencil · notebook | phone · computer · camera · headphones | keys · wallet · glasses · watch · umbrella · bag |",
      "",
      "**Singular y plural:** *a pen → two pens · a key → keys · a bag → bags*.",
      "",
      "**Siempre en plural:** *glasses, headphones, keys* (normalmente) y *trousers*. Se dice **My glasses are on the table** (con *are*). Para hablar de uno solo: *a pair of glasses*.",
      "",
      "**a / an:** *a pen, a notebook* · *an umbrella, an apple* (según el **sonido**: vocal → an).",
      "",
      "**watch vs clock:** *watch* = reloj de pulsera (y el verbo 'mirar'); *clock* = reloj de pared o de mesa.",
      "",
      "**Ojo, falso amigo:** *carpet* es **alfombra**; carpeta = *folder*.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *pencil* /ˈpensl/ · *computer* /kəmˈpjuːtə/ · *umbrella* /ʌmˈbrelə/ · *wallet* /ˈwɒlɪt/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "My glasses is new.",
        "right": "My glasses are new.",
        "note": "Glasses es plural."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I've got a umbrella.",
        "right": "I've got an umbrella.",
        "note": "Umbrella empieza con sonido vocálico: an."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": [
      {
        "word": "carpet",
        "es_false": "carpeta",
        "real": "alfombra",
        "note": "La carpeta se dice folder."
      }
    ]
  },
